            {
                id defects.serializer-escaping
                title "Serializer performs no escaping and never widens delimiters"
                priority 1
                sealed true
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-07-29T17:58:47.961767Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @decision
                        text "Scope this node to structural corruption only, not to the serialiser's documented canonicalisation. In scope: content that re-parses as different structure — a backtick inside a CodeSpan (widen the fence), a closing-fence-shaped line inside a CodeBlock (widen the fence), `|` inside a table cell (escape), `\"` inside a link title (escape or requote), and inline text whose characters would re-parse as markup in that position. Prefer minimal positional escaping; over-escaping is its own defect. Explicitly out of scope, left as the canonicalisation `editing.serialize.round-trip` already enumerates honestly: `List::tight` dropped so lists emit loose, `FootnoteDefinition` label/number/backref_count dropped, `TaskItem` always emitting a bullet marker, and Subscript/Superscript emitting HTML. Those lose node metadata; they do not corrupt structure. Tests assert the span-erased AST survives a serialise/re-parse cycle, not exact bytes."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-07-29T18:01:24.010531Z
