            {
                id defects.editor-span-drift
                title "Editor spans drift against the un-normalised buffer; cursor never remapped"
                priority 2
                sealed true
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-07-29T17:58:28.358197Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @decision
                        text "Resolve by normalising on ingest: `set_source` and `edit` store the text after `normalize_chunk` (CRLF/CR to LF, NUL to U+FFFD), so \"spans index the stored buffer\" holds by construction rather than via a translation layer every caller must remember. Rejected the alternative of keeping the raw buffer and mapping spans back to raw offsets: it preserves the caller's exact bytes but requires translating every span the parser emits, including deep inline spans, where a missed site is a silent wrong-offset bug rather than a compile error. Accepted cost: EditableDocument no longer echoes the caller's exact bytes — a CRLF document reads back LF-normalised — and callers supplying byte offsets must do so against the normalised text."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-07-29T18:02:07.923281Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Todo → Done (nplan complete)"
                    }
                )
            }

            {
                id defects.ansi-feature-gaps
                title "ColorDepth inert, colon colour forms unsupported, dim/strike dropped"
                priority 2
                sealed true
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-07-29T18:00:33.320761Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Three of the four items are fixed: ColorDepth now genuinely downgrades (quantisation added to ansi_style.rs reusing the existing palette, routed through a new AnsiAdapter::sgr_color), the colon-delimited T.416 colour forms parse alongside the semicolon forms, and `dim` now reaches the grid. Note `dim` was never a dependency limitation — the in-code comment claiming so was wrong; vt100 0.16.2 exposes Cell::dim() at cell.rs:155 and it had simply never been wired up. `strike` genuinely cannot be fixed at this version: there is no TEXT_MODE_STRIKE bit, no accessor, and Screen::sgr has no arm for SGR 9, so the attribute is discarded inside the emulator before a snapshot could observe it. 0.16.2 is the latest published release; only the vt100-ctt 0.17 fork is newer. Left as a documented limitation in ansi.term.style-mapping rather than faked. A related behaviour difference is now specified: vt100 treats intensity as one exclusive slot, so a snapshotted cell is never both bold and dim, unlike the byte-stream path where they are independent. Follow-up: the rule id `ansi.adapter.color-depth-inert` is now actively misleading since the field is no longer inert, and wants renaming."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-07-29T18:02:17.754386Z
