                        text "Closing with 28 of 203 mw rules still impl-only, deliberately. mw tested coverage went 128/203 (63%) to 175/203 (86%) — 46 rules closed by 112 new tests; the 47th was closed concurrently by the highlighter session. Configured suite 837 to 914 passing.\n\nZero were closed by annotating a pre-existing test. Every mod tests in the tree was swept. The ~12 url_safety.rs tests and the markdawn-android ones that an earlier review flagged as unannotated had already been annotated earlier in this session, so that free coverage was gone before this pass started.\n\nThe residual 28 break down as: 16 uikit (whole subtree is cfg(target_os = \"ios\"), never executes under cargo nextest, and all 16 additionally need live Apple runtime objects — UIFont, NSURLSession, UIStackView, CoreSVG, UIColor trait collections — not merely an iOS build); 9 iced (need a text::Renderer + svg::Renderer instance, a widget Tree/Shell, or an event loop; iced's own null renderer sets Paragraph = () so it cannot exercise any cosmic-text path); 2 ffi (ffi.host.wasm-bindgen is entirely about generated JS glue and needs a wasm-pack/node harness; ffi.ownership.retained-objc needs a live UIKit runtime to observe +1 retain counts); 1 core (core.error.location, whose body is wrong about the implementation — see defects.spec-bodies-inaccurate).\n\nThree of those 28 are actionable rather than blocked and are filed as defects.uikit-syntax-logic-apple-bound. One, iced.renderer.parse-failure-empty, describes unreachable code. Deliberately no uikit tests were written: a test that type-checks but never executes would report coverage that does not exist."
