            {
                id defects.uikit-image-allowlist-bypass
                title "UIKit image path never applies the URL allow-list"
                priority 1
                sealed true
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-07-29T17:57:55.093342Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "`try_load_image` (src/adapter/uikit/render.rs:799) never calls `is_safe_image_url`, while every other image-emitting adapter does — vdom.rs:852, dioxus.rs:760, iced/render.rs:1260. Consequences: every `data:` media type is decoded rather than only `data:image/*`, so the narrowing documented at url_safety.rs:71-91 does not apply here; the SVG branch selects on `parsed.mime.contains(\"svg\")`, a substring test over the whole header including parameters, so `data:text/html;charset=svg,<svg…>` routes attacker bytes into the private CoreSVG parser under a non-image media type; and there is no control-character rejection, which `is_safe_url` performs specifically to stop `jav\\tascript:` smuggling. Network fetch is gated by a literal http:// / https:// prefix test, so smuggling cannot reach NSURLSession today, but that is incidental rather than the allow-list. Current behaviour is documented as-is in `uikit.media.image-source`; wiring the allow-list in is a behaviour change, which is this node."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-07-29T19:12:26.785785Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Todo → Done (nplan complete)"
