            {
                id defects.uikit-svg-sanitiser-bypass
                title "UIKit SVG rasterisation bypasses the sanitiser"
                priority 1
                sealed true
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-07-29T17:57:58.599439Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Nothing under src/adapter/uikit/ references `svg_sanitize`. Three paths hand attacker-influenced bytes straight to `CGSVGDocumentCreateFromData`, a private Apple API resolved via dlsym: raw markdown HTML chunks that sniff as SVG (`try_render_svg_html`, block and inline), `data:` URIs whose header contains \"svg\", and remote fetch responses that sniff as SVG (`image_loader::handle_completion`). The last is sharpest — payload is whatever an arbitrary http(s) server returns, MAX_SVG_BYTES (5 MB) is not applied on that path, and the only bound is MAX_SVG_DIMENSION (4096 pt), checked after CoreSVG has already parsed. Caveat for weighing severity: CoreSVG rasterises to a UIImage rather than into a live DOM, so script execution — the sanitiser's primary target — is not obviously reachable. Residual exposure is unsanitised unbounded input into an undocumented private parser, plus whatever external-resource fetching CoreSVG performs for `<image href>` / `<use href>`, which the sanitiser's URL allow-list normally gates. Current behaviour documented as-is in `uikit.media.svg-raster`."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-07-29T19:12:29.708089Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Todo → Done (nplan complete)"
                    }
                )
            }

            {
                id defects.uikit-diagram-engine-output-unsanitised
                title "UIKit diagram views pass raw engine SVG to the rasteriser"
                priority 1
                sealed true
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-07-29T19:12:16.986668Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Found while fixing defects.uikit-svg-sanitiser-bypass; same class, separate site. views/graphviz.rs:23, views/pikchr.rs:23 and views/typst.rs:23 call the engines directly (markdawn_graphviz::render_dot_to_svg, crate::pikchr_render::render, crate::typst::render) and hand the output straight to render_svg — no sanitiser, no MAX_SVG_BYTES. Every other adapter funnels engine output through lib.rs::finalize_diagram_svg, which sanitises and outlines text. Engine input is attacker-controlled markdown, so the exposure is the same class as the three paths already fixed. Left alone deliberately: it is governed by uikit.diagram.view-factory, which that task was not authorised to bump, and routing through render_pikchr_to_svg / render_graphviz_to_svg / render_typst_to_svg would additionally apply text-to-path outlining — a visual change that should be a deliberate decision rather than a side effect of a security fix. math.rs:56 also uses raw render_svg but on mathml-core output from our own renderer, which is not attacker-shaped in the same way. Decide whether these views should use the shared finalize path (accepting the outlining change) or gain a sanitise-only variant."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-07-29T21:53:59.62493Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @decision
                        text "Fixed by routing all three views through the crate's shared entry points — render_graphviz_to_svg / render_pikchr_to_svg / render_typst_to_svg, each of which is finalize_diagram_svg(engine(source)): MAX_SVG_BYTES cap, then svg_sanitize::sanitize_svg, then svg_text_to_paths. Operator accepted the text-to-path outlining consequence.\n\nUsed render_svg rather than render_svg_sanitized: by that point the bytes ARE the sanitiser's output, so the wrapper would re-run html5ever parse + allow-list + serialise over the crate's own just-sanitised document on the main thread per diagram — cost with no new guarantee. Honest nuance recorded: the cap inside finalize_diagram_svg is applied pre-outline, so outlining could in principle push the result past MAX_SVG_BYTES where the wrapper's cap would have caught it. That is what vdom, dioxus and iced all already do, so it is a pre-existing crate-wide property rather than something this fix introduced.\n\nmath.rs:56 deliberately left on render_svg, on two independent grounds. Generator shape: mathml-core builds an SVG DOM with xmlem and serialises it, only ever emitting svg/g/path/text/rect with numeric coordinates and colour values, with escaping done by the serialiser rather than string concatenation — there is no element or attribute in that alphabet that can carry script or a URL. The diagram engines are the opposite: string builders that deliberately forward document-supplied attributes, and graphviz turns URL= straight into xlink:href. Consistency: all four adapters treat mathml output as trusted and none sanitise it, so UIKit's math path was never the outlier — the diagram views were. Caveat for the future: if mathml-core ever emits <a xlink:href> or raw passthrough, the conclusion flips for all four adapters at once and belongs as a crate-wide change, not a UIKit patch.\n\nuikit.diagram.view-factory bumped v0 to v1 across the marker and four annotation sites. uikit.media.svg-raster deliberately not bumped — the entry-point split it describes is unchanged and its text stays literally true."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-07-29T21:54:36.84092Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Todo → Done (nplan complete)"
                    }
                )
            }

